    "usage": {
      "activation": [
        "No shell activation is required for an APT installation; use /usr/bin/patchelf.",
        "The functional check needs Python 3 and a working C compiler named cc. It builds a private executable and shared library and runs each edited variant."
      ],
      "documentation": [
        "https://packages.ubuntu.com/noble/patchelf",
        "https://github.com/NixOS/patchelf",
        "https://github.com/NixOS/patchelf/blob/0.18.0/README.md"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "command": "dpkg-query -L {package_name}",
          "description": "List the files registered by the system package manager."
        },
        {
          "command": "patchelf --print-interpreter ./program\npatchelf --print-needed ./program\npatchelf --print-rpath ./program",
          "description": "Inspect the dynamic loader and direct shared-library names before changing a binary."
        },
        {
          "command": "patchelf --set-rpath '$ORIGIN/../lib' ./bin/program",
          "description": "Use a library directory relative to the executable; single quotes preserve the literal $ORIGIN token."
        },
        {
          "command": "patchelf --replace-needed libold.so libnew.so ./program",
          "description": "Replace one DT_NEEDED entry after arranging the compatible replacement library."
        },
        {
          "command": "patchelf --print-soname ./libexample.so",
          "description": "Read the declared identity of a shared library."
        },
        {
          "command": "cpg packages check apt.patchelf --kind functional",
          "description": "Run loader-failure, RUNPATH, relocation, NEEDED and SONAME checks on private fixtures."
        }
      ],
      "locations": [
        {
          "label": "Prepared material",
          "path": "{assets}/apt/patchelf_0.18.0-1.1build1_amd64.deb",
          "purpose": "Independent verified source, input, data or upstream distribution."
        },
        {
          "label": "System package files",
          "path": "/var/lib/dpkg/info/patchelf.list",
          "purpose": "Ask dpkg-query -L for the actual installed file list, including multiarch packages."
        },
        {
          "label": "ELF editing command",
          "path": "{prefix}/bin/patchelf",
          "purpose": "Inspect or modify ELF loader metadata; pass the specific executable or shared library path."
        },
        {
          "label": "Manual page",
          "path": "{prefix}/share/man/man1/patchelf.1.gz",
          "purpose": "Installed command options; read with man patchelf."
        },
        {
          "label": "Package notices",
          "path": "{prefix}/share/doc/patchelf",
          "purpose": "Distribution copyright and package documentation."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Ubuntu 0.18.0-1.1build1 is the pinned distribution package; patchelf --version reports upstream 0.18.0.",
        "Qualification covers generated x86_64 ELF fixtures. Editing metadata is not proof that an arbitrary binary remains runnable: execute the edited program with its intended libraries and deployment layout.",
        "The check verifies two expected missing-library failures and four successful execution variants, including a moved directory tree and a renamed DT_NEEDED dependency.",
        "The wrapper delegates installation/removal to APT. Querying resources and running these private-file checks do not themselves perform an APT transaction."
      ],
      "summary": "Inspect and edit ELF dynamic-loader metadata: origin-relative RPATH/RUNPATH, DT_NEEDED shared-library names, interpreter path, and shared-library SONAME."
    },
